.Dd February 1, 2026
.Dt KFREE 9
.Os Substrate
.Sh NAME
.Nm kfree
.Nd free kernel memory allocated with kmalloc
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In vm/vm_kmem.h
.Ft void
.Fn kfree "void *ptr" "size_t size"
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Fn kfree
function frees a block of memory previously allocated by
.Fn kmalloc
or
.Fn kzalloc .
.Pp
The arguments are:
.Bl -tag -width size
.It Fa ptr
The pointer to the memory block to be freed.
If
.Fa ptr
is
.Dv NULL ,
no action is performed.
.It Fa size
The size of the memory block being freed, in bytes.
This must match the size passed to the original allocation call.
.El
.Sh RETURN VALUES
The
.Fn kfree
function returns no value.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr kmalloc 9 ,
.Xr kzalloc 9 ,
.Xr kmem_init 9
.Sh HISTORY
The
.Fn kfree
function first appeared in Substrate.
.Sh AUTHORS
.An -nosplit
The Substrate Project
